    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "It is a very impoverished area, but people that love our congressional district. And it's an area that Governor Kehoe cares a great deal about. In fact, his farm is in our congressional district. And he loves to spend a lot of time there. He goes around and tells people he chose to be a first-generation farmer. Well, that farm is Delps County, Missouri. And so if you look at just the people involved in all the activities, so many constituents from the 8th District. My key hoe is Lieutenant Governor, and I know as Governor, knows every one of our counties in Southeastern Missouri, and he knows the issues that we deal with. It's quite interesting and Ozark Appalachia is what I refer, but you know what? I think with the right policies and the right partnerships with the state and the federal level, we're going to be able to transform that area. I want to make sure my people see economic prosperity and growth and we'll get it done. One",
